WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.100
Everything on My day.

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:15.033
My day: where every morning starts. Today's date, how many appointments you have today, anything overdue and how many crews are on site. Everything on this screen is about you and today.

00:00:15.533 --> 00:00:28.900
Search everything. Type a name, phone, street, or an EST-, JOB- or INV- number and pick the result to open it. ⌘K (Ctrl+K) jumps here from any screen.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:36.567
Help. Ask how to do something in your own words. It finds the tour that fits and shows you on the screen, like this one.

00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:47.300
Notifications. New assignments, wins and payments for you. The red number counts the unread ones. Click one to open it; Mark all read clears them.

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:58.800
Crews out today. How many crews are on a job today, out of all your crews. If you see money, this month's wins and the value of estimates out with customers sit beside it.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:10.867
New customer. Opens the New customer form right here: name, phones, address, salesperson, and the first appointment if you like. Saving opens the new customer.

00:01:11.367 --> 00:01:21.133
New appointment. Book a visit, a phone call or a task for anyone. It goes straight onto that person's day. The Appointments tours walk every field.

00:01:21.633 --> 00:01:28.867
Schedule. Opens the Schedule board: crews down the side, days across, and the sold work waiting for a date.

00:01:29.367 --> 00:01:38.800
Estimates out. Sent estimates still waiting on the customer: the value, or the count if you don't see money. Click the box to open Estimates.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:47.200
Won this month. Estimates won since the 1st of the month and how many jobs they made. Click the box to open Jobs.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:56.000
To schedule. Pieces of sold work with no crew or start day yet. Click the box to open the Schedule and give them a date.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:08.000
Overdue invoices. What customers owe past the due date, and on how many invoices. Click the box to open Invoices. People who don't see money get Crews out today here.

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:17.533
My day. Your appointments and tasks for today, with anything overdue at the top in red. Add books a new one for you or for someone else.

00:02:18.033 --> 00:02:30.400
Open an appointment. Each line shows the time, what it's for, the customer, place and phone, and the type. A camera means the visit sent notes or photos. Click a line to open it.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:43.167
The appointment. When, with whom, the customer (click the name to open them), phone, address and office notes. Below: notes, measurements and photos saved on the visit from the phone.

00:02:43.667 --> 00:02:56.767
Edit, visit done, mark done. Edit changes it. Visit done · estimate pending keeps an estimate visit open as the reminder to write the quote. Mark done closes it. The tour presses none of them.

00:02:57.267 --> 00:03:01.667
Close it. The X closes the appointment without changing anything.

00:03:02.167 --> 00:03:10.367
Edit from the list. The pencil opens the appointment's form straight away, to change the day, time, person or details.

00:03:10.867 --> 00:03:18.233
Mark it done. The tick marks it done and takes it off your day. Use it once the visit, call or task has happened.

00:03:18.733 --> 00:03:27.867
Next 7 days. Your appointments for the coming week, day by day, so you can plan office time. The lines work the same as in My day.

00:03:28.367 --> 00:03:40.433
What needs you. Cards here appear only when there is something to do: New from the website, Waiting on a permit (the township hasn't approved yet) and Waiting on a quote (visit done, no estimate).

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:52.667
New from the website. Website requests waiting for someone. Accept makes the lead (or finds the existing customer) plus a ticket, and opens them. All opens Marketing.

00:03:53.167 --> 00:04:04.767
Follow-ups. Sent estimates with no answer yet: click one to open it; Sent or Called records the follow-up. When none are due it says the automatic follow-ups are handling them.

00:04:05.267 --> 00:04:15.233
On site today. Which crew is on which job today, with the customer, place and "day 3 of 5" on longer jobs. Click a line to open the job.

00:04:15.733 --> 00:04:25.133
Automations. Messages the automations sent today, how many are waiting to go and any that failed (red). Click it to open Automations.

00:04:25.633 --> 00:04:34.000
Missed clock-outs. Shows up when someone on a crew forgot to clock out. Fix it on Timesheets before payroll: click it to go there.

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:41.867
Fleet. Truck problems the crews reported from the phone, and trucks overdue for service. Click it to open Fleet.

00:04:42.367 --> 00:04:50.333
Latest across the business. The eight latest things that happened across all customers. Click a name to open that customer.

00:04:50.833 --> 00:04:56.433
That's it. You can play this tour in the app any time: press Help, and ask in your own words.
